# Nothing that is not this project's own source belongs in an image build context.
#
# The proprietary client assets are the important entry here. `private-client/` is
# the archived original game client and `web/` is its prepared derivative; both are
# excluded so they can never be copied by a `COPY` that forgot to be specific, and
# the send to the daemon stays small. The runtime mounts the prepared client
# instead, which is why the image has an empty `web/`.
private-client/
web/
maps/
captures/
state/
.env
.env.*

# Build tooling and its caches. None of it is needed to run the service, and
# `node_modules` in particular would add ~100 MB (and, at 97% disk on the host this
# was verified on, would simply not fit).
node_modules/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/

# Development-only material.
tests/
docs/
.github/
.git/
.githooks/
*.log
*.pid
*.proof.png
*.png
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.har

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
